                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Gonococcal urethritis produces copious purulent discharge with shorter incubation (2–7 days); chlamydial urethritis has scant mucoid discharge with longer incubation (7–21 days). NAAT testing on urethral swab or first-void urine differentiates the two."
